Challenge 3: Polymorphic Notification Engine
Scenario: Your company sends alerts via Email and SMS. Next month, they want to add WhatsApp. If you use if/else checks, you'll have to rewrite your whole app later.

Task: Use an Interface to make the NotificationManager "plugin-based."


// 1. Create an interface named 'MessageService' with a method 'send(String msg)'

class EmailService implements MessageService {
    public void send(String msg) { System.out.println("Sending Email: " + msg); }
}

class SMSService implements MessageService {
    public void send(String msg) { System.out.println("Sending SMS: " + msg); }
}

public class NotificationManager {
    // 2. This method should take the INTERFACE as a parameter, not the specific class
    public void processAlert(MessageService service, String message) {
        service.send(message);
    }
}